			"Message": "feat(desktop): Add Tauri configuration and workbench services\n\nThis commit expands the Wind framework with essential services for Tauri desktop integration. The TauriConfigurationService replaces Electron's configuration system, providing scope-based configuration (APPLICATION, WORKSPACE, PROFILE) with change event propagation. The TauriWorkbench implements a full workbench layout for Tauri, managing parts like titlebar, sidebar, and editor. Additionally, the WindInstantiationService is enhanced with advanced cycle detection using depth-first search, comprehensive error handling, and service lifecycle management. These foundational components support the seamless replacement of Electron with Tauri in the VSCode workbench environment.",
			"SHA": "2da33c922177c51fc48c8dfd9e1cb13855c3364b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T05:40:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				347,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(instantiation): add WindInstantiationService for VSCode workbench integration\n\nThis commit introduces a comprehensive dependency injection framework designed to replace VSCode's InstantiationService with Wind-compatible implementation. The service provides:\n\n- Service collection management with registration and retrieval capabilities\n- Dependency graph resolution with cycle detection\n- Service lifecycle management including disposal\n- Performance tracing for debugging and optimization\n- Child service hierarchy support\n\nThe implementation follows VSCode's architecture (`vs/platform/instantiation/common/instantiationService.ts`) while adding Wind-specific enhancements. Key features include:\n\n- SyncDescriptor for lazy service instantiation\n- ServiceIdentifier type safety\n- Graph-based dependency resolution\n- Strict mode for error handling\n- Tracing capabilities for performance monitoring\n\nThis foundational service enables proper dependency injection patterns throughout the Wind codebase, supporting future workbench integration and service modularization.",
			"SHA": "fc4f144f62e932602460e6b7dd5c36a576f0a9c6"
		},
